/**
 * RuleText.gs - the hostel brochures, as text, in the repository.
 *
 * WHY THIS IS A SOURCE FILE AND NOT AN UPLOAD
 * -------------------------------------------
 * Nineteen comments across this project cite "the brochure" for a rule, and
 * for most of its life the brochure was not in the repository - it lived on
 * somebody's desk. A reader could not check a claim, and the assistant could
 * not answer until an administrator remembered to upload a PDF.
 *
 * The admission brochures are fixed for the session. They are reference data,
 * exactly like the pincode table in Geo.gs, so they belong in version control
 * where a diff shows precisely what changed when the university reissues them.
 *
 * Generated by chunking the two 2026-27 PDFs through RuleBook.chunkText. To
 * refresh for a new session, re-run that against the new PDFs and replace this
 * file wholesale - do not hand-edit it, or the text stops matching the source
 * document it claims to quote.
 *
 * Each entry is [heading, text]. Arrays rather than objects because at 248
 * passages the key names alone would cost several kilobytes to no purpose.
 */

var RULE_TEXT = {
  session: "2026-27",
  sources: [
    {
      sourceRef: "Boys brochure",
